###  http://www.semanticweb.org/najma/ontologies/homecredit/hasInstallmentToIncomeRatio
:hasInstallmentToIncomeRatio rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                             rdfs:domain <https://spec.edmcouncil.org/fibo/ontology/LOAN/LoansGeneral/LoanApplications/LoanApplication> ;
                             rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
                             dcterms:source "Bank for International Settlements, CGFS Papers No. 69, 'Macroprudential policies to mitigate housing market risks' (borrower-income-based limits: DSTI, DTI). https://www.bis.org/publ/cgfs69.pdf"@en ,
                                            "Home Credit Group, HomeCredit_columns_description.csv (competition 'Home Credit Default Risk', Kaggle), application_train.csv, columns AMT_ANNUITY, AMT_INCOME_TOTAL. https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/home-credit-default-risk/data"@en ,
                                            "PADK OJK No. 2 Tahun 2026 (BNPL): perbandingan pembayaran pokok dan manfaat ekonomi terhadap penghasilan paling tinggi 40% pada 2027-2028 dan 30% sejak 2029 (as reported by Fortune Indonesia, https://www.fortuneidn.com/finance/batas-usia-penghasilan-debitur-paylater-dibatasi-ojk-demi-jaga-kua-00-5mjpg-ld1v0c; verify against the official text)."@en ,
                                            "Sher, G. (2023). Borrower-Based Macroprudential Instruments in Germany. IMF Selected Issues Paper SIP/2023/060 (definitions of DSTI, DTI and LTI). https://www.imf.org/-/media/files/publications/selected-issues-papers/2023/english/sipea2023060.pdf"@en ,
                                            "Surat Edaran OJK No. 19/SEOJK.06/2025 tentang Penyelenggaraan LPBBTI (turunan POJK No. 40 Tahun 2024): penerima dana minimal 18 tahun atau telah menikah; rasio utang terhadap penghasilan paling tinggi 40% pada 2025 dan 30% mulai 2026 (as reported by Bisnis.com, https://finansial.bisnis.com/read/20260112/563/1943510/tahun-ini-batas-maksimal-kredit-pinjol-diperketat-jadi-30-dari-gaji; verify against the official text)."@en ;
                             :rangeSource "Bank for International Settlements, CGFS Papers No. 69, 'Macroprudential policies to mitigate housing market risks' (borrower-income-based limits: DSTI, DTI). https://www.bis.org/publ/cgfs69.pdf"@en ,
                                          "Bisnis.com (2025), 'Perhatian! SLIK Tak Jadi Satu-satunya Faktor Penilaian KPR Bank': installment-to-income usually capped at 30-40%. https://finansial.bisnis.com/read/20250626/55/1888474/perhatian-slik-tak-jadi-satu-satunya-faktor-penilaian-kpr-bank"@en ,
                                          "PADK OJK No. 2 Tahun 2026 (BNPL): perbandingan pembayaran pokok dan manfaat ekonomi terhadap penghasilan paling tinggi 40% pada 2027-2028 dan 30% sejak 2029 (as reported by Fortune Indonesia, https://www.fortuneidn.com/finance/batas-usia-penghasilan-debitur-paylater-dibatasi-ojk-demi-jaga-kua-00-5mjpg-ld1v0c; verify against the official text)."@en ,
                                          "Sher, G. (2023). Borrower-Based Macroprudential Instruments in Germany. IMF Selected Issues Paper SIP/2023/060 (definitions of DSTI, DTI and LTI). https://www.imf.org/-/media/files/publications/selected-issues-papers/2023/english/sipea2023060.pdf"@en ,
                                          "Surat Edaran OJK No. 19/SEOJK.06/2025 tentang Penyelenggaraan LPBBTI (turunan POJK No. 40 Tahun 2024): penerima dana minimal 18 tahun atau telah menikah; rasio utang terhadap penghasilan paling tinggi 40% pada 2025 dan 30% mulai 2026 (as reported by Bisnis.com, https://finansial.bisnis.com/read/20260112/563/1943510/tahun-ini-batas-maksimal-kredit-pinjol-diperketat-jadi-30-dari-gaji; verify against the official text)."@en ;
                             :valueRange "Observed range: 0 to no fixed maximum. Regulatory/literature threshold: OJK caps on debt/payments relative to income: online lending (LPBBTI) 40% in 2025 and 30% from 2026 (SEOJK 19/2025); BNPL 40% in 2027-2028 and 30% from 2029 (PADK 2/2026); bank mortgage practice commonly 30-40% (Bisnis, 2025). Note: No published range for this derived ratio: compute annuity/income from your data. Income and annuity periods are not stated in the dictionary, so align periods before comparing with the OJK caps."@en ;
                             rdfs:comment "Represents the ratio of installment payments to income when calculated as hasAnnuityAmount / hasIncomeAmount. OJK thresholds are reference comparisons for the applicable lending contexts, not general requirements for all consumer loans. Any threshold must follow the applicable period and regulation."@en ;
                             skos:definition "Ratio of the loan's periodic installment (annuity) to the applicant's income. In IMF/ESRB/BIS terminology an installment-to-income measure is a debt-service-to-income (DSTI) ratio, whereas a DTI ratio uses outstanding debt balances. The Home Credit dictionary does not state the period of income or annuity, so comparison with OJK ratio caps (stated against income) needs a consistent period."@en .


